3. SUMMARY IN PLAIN LANGUAGE

- We do not look at, record, or store the websites you visit, the apps you
  use, or the content of anything you send or receive through the VPN.
- To run your account we store your username, your password (in protected
  form), and a device identifier so your account can be bound to your
  device.
- Our servers process the technical information needed to route your
  traffic and to operate the service.
- The App shows advertising supplied by Google AdMob. AdMob and its partners
  may use your advertising ID and device information to show ads, including
  personalized ads where you have consented.
- The App uses Google Firebase for basic usage analytics and push
  notifications.
- You can ask us to delete your account and your data at any time. See
  Section 14.


4. INFORMATION WE COLLECT

4.1 Information you give us

  - Account username and password. When you register or sign in, your
    username and password are sent to our servers to create or access your
    account. Your credentials are also stored on your device so the App can
    reconnect without asking you again.
  - Support messages. If you contact us for help, we receive whatever you
    choose to send us (for example your message and any diagnostic log you
    decide to attach).

4.2 Device and app information

  - Device identifier. The App generates an identifier derived from your
    device's Android ID. This identifier is sent to our servers and used to
    bind your account to your device, for example to enforce the number of
    devices allowed per account. It is not used to track you across other
    apps or websites.
  - Device name and model, operating system version, and App version. Used
    to show you your registered devices, to let you remove a device from
    your account, and to diagnose technical problems.
  - Your IP address, as seen by our servers, is used to establish the VPN
    connection.

4.3 VPN connection information

When you connect, our servers process the technical information required to
operate the service, such as:

  - the server you connected to;
  - the date and time of the connection and its duration;
  - the amount of data transferred, used to apply any data or time limits
    attached to your plan;
  - connection errors and protocol diagnostics.

This information is used to run the service, to enforce plan limits, to
prevent abuse, and to keep the network working. We do not use it to build a
profile of the websites you visit.

4.4 Advertising information

The App displays advertising provided by Google AdMob (banner,
interstitial, rewarded, and app-open ads). To serve ads, Google and its
advertising partners may collect and process:

  - your advertising ID (a resettable identifier provided by Android);
  - your IP address and approximate location derived from it;
  - device information (device model, operating system, language);
  - information about your interaction with ads (for example, whether an ad
    was shown, viewed, or clicked).

The App also includes Google's User Messaging Platform, which asks for and
records your consent choices for advertising where the law requires
(for example in the European Economic Area and the United Kingdom). Your
consent choices are stored on your device.

4.5 Analytics and diagnostics

The App includes Google Firebase Analytics and Firebase Cloud Messaging.
Firebase Analytics collects general usage and device information (such as
app launches, screens used, device model, and country-level location) to
help us understand how the App is used. Firebase Cloud Messaging provides
the technical channel used to deliver app notifications. This data is
processed by Google on our behalf.

The App also keeps a technical log on your device (connection events and
server addresses). This log stays on your device. It is only shared with us
if you choose to copy it and send it to us for support.


5. INFORMATION WE DO NOT COLLECT

  - We do not log the websites you visit, the apps you use, or the search
    terms you enter.
  - We do not inspect, record, or store the content of your traffic, such as
    messages, emails, files, photos, or the pages you load.
  - We do not record the DNS queries you make through the VPN for the
    purpose of profiling you.
  - We do not sell your personal information to anyone.
  - We do not collect your precise GPS location.
  - We do not read your contacts, photos, messages, or call history.


6. PERMISSIONS THE APP REQUESTS

  - Internet and network state. Required to create the VPN connection.
  - Wi-Fi state. Required to detect your connection and to support the
    Wi-Fi tethering feature.
  - Foreground service. Required so the VPN stays connected while the App is
    in the background, with a visible notification.
  - Notifications. Used to show the VPN status notification and service
    messages.
  - Start on boot. Used to restore your VPN session after a restart, if you
    enabled that option.
  - Advertising ID. Used by Google AdMob to serve advertising.
  - Storage (Android 12 and older only). Used to save and load configuration
    files.

The App does not request access to your location, camera, microphone,
contacts, SMS, or call logs.


7. HOW WE USE INFORMATION

  - To create and manage your account and to bind it to your devices.
  - To provide the VPN service and route your traffic through our servers.
  - To enforce plan limits, including time or data allowances.
  - To detect, prevent, and fix abuse, fraud, and technical faults.
  - To display advertising that supports the free version of the App.
  - To send service notifications.
  - To comply with legal obligations.


